            <history xml:id="history_93dc3e4e">
               <p xml:id="idm70">August von Kotzebue's play "Die beiden kleinen Auvergnaten" (1813) had had its first Danish performance at The Royal Theatre in Copenhagen in N.T.' Bruun's translation in 1815. The fourth performance, which took place on Sunday 20 April 1834, was a special one: it included additional songs by H.P. Holst with music of different composers, performed by pupils of the Academy of Music. King Christian VIII attended the event.</p>
